---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="Use decod.ing offline"
  description="Install the free web app or run the local CLI from source."
>
  <section class="page-hero container narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">On this device</span><h1>Keep the workbench close.</h1>
    <p>
      Use your browser’s Install app action. On iPhone or iPad, choose Share → Add to Home Screen.
      Open the tools you need once online to cache their local parsers.
    </p>
    <a class="button" href="/tools/">Open the 47 local tools</a>
    <h2>Command line from source</h2>
    <p>
      The CLI is available in the source repository; it is not published to npm. With Node 22 and
      pnpm 10, install dependencies and pipe synthetic text into the CLI:
    </p>
    <pre><code>pnpm install
printf '%s' 'eyJvayI6dHJ1ZX0=' | pnpm cli</code></pre>
    <h2>Desktop builds</h2>
    <p>Signed desktop downloads are not available yet. Use the web app or source CLI today.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
